+Good question @PrinceOfEgypt. This PR hooks TitledDescriptionPane, so the warning shows across every Coldcard selection/import surface (file/QR import, airgapped keystore, USB, export) — but you're right that it does not fire when an already-created Coldcard wallet is simply opened/loaded.
+A load-time acknowledgment (e.g. "I confirm I regenerated a secure seed on fixed firmware or with ≥50 verified dice rolls") is a good idea, but it's a meaningfully larger change — persisted per-wallet acknowledgment state + a dialog/banner in the wallet-open path — and I'd want it built and tested locally before proposing it (I flagged in the PR that I couldn't run a full Gradle build here). Happy to open it as a separate follow-up if @craigraw thinks the load-time prompt is worth adding; this PR keeps the scope to the additive, low-risk selection-time warning.
